        P("The Gram stain also tells you shape and arrangement. <b>Cocci</b> come as clusters (staphylococci), chains (streptococci), diplococci or tetrads. <b>Bacilli</b> come as diplobacilli, chains, coccobacilli or fusiform (pointed ends). <b>Spirochetes</b> are spiral. In a sputum or wound sample it also judges specimen quality and helps separate colonization from infection."),
